│   Save and organize       │ ── Template functions ──                                                                                                         │
│   Environments            │ Write {{ $name(argument, ...) }} in any field. An argument is a 'literal',                                                       │
│   Secrets and auth        │ a number, a variable (user_id, $uuid, $processEnv.NAME) or another call.                                                         │
│   Chain requests          │ Calls nest up to 8 levels. A random call keeps one value for the whole send.                                                     │
│   Read a response         │ An unknown function, a wrong number of arguments or a bad value leaves the                                                       │
│   Import and export       │ placeholder unresolved, and the send tells you why.                                                                              │
│   gRPC call               │   $uuidBytes(uuid)              the 16 bytes of a UUID, base64; hyphens are optional, any case                                   │
│   Streams (WS, SSE, MQTT) │   $uuidFromBytes(base64)        the UUID text of 16 bytes (lowercase, with hyphens)                                              │
│   MCP tools               │   $uuidV5(namespace, name)      the name-based UUID v5: namespace is a UUID, name the text                                       │
│   Run a folder            │   $uuidV7()                     a time-ordered UUID v7; random                                                                   │
│   Customize               │   $ulid()                       a ULID (26 Crockford base32 characters); random                                                  │
│ Keys                      │   $hexBytes(hex)                the bytes of an even number of hex digits, base64                                                │
│   All keys                │   $bytesHex(base64)             the bytes in lowercase hex                                                                       │
│   Global                  │   $base64(text)                 standard base64 of the UTF-8 text                                                                │
│   Sidebar tree            │   $base64Url(text)              URL-safe base64 of the UTF-8 text, no padding                                                    │
│   Text editing            │   $base64Decode(base64)         the decoded text; the bytes must be UTF-8                                                        │
│   Tables                  │   $hex(text)                    lowercase hex of the UTF-8 text                                                                  │
│   Response                │   $urlEncode(text)              the text percent-encoded as a query component                                                    │
│   Query (jq)              │   $md5(text)                    the MD5 of the text, in lowercase hex                                                            │
│   Dialogs                 │   $sha1(text)                   the SHA-1 of the text, in lowercase hex                                                          │
│   Fixed keys              │   $sha256(text)                 the SHA-256 of the text, in lowercase hex                                                        │
│   Symbols                 │   $sha512(text)                 the SHA-512 of the text, in lowercase hex                                                        │
│   Commands                │   $hmacSha256(key, text)        the HMAC-SHA256 of the text, in lowercase hex                                                    │
│ Functions                 │   $hmacSha256Base64(key, text)  the HMAC-SHA256 of the text, in base64                                                           │
│▌  Template functions      │   $timeAdd(time, duration)      an RFC 3339 time plus a duration such as 90s, 1h30m or -2d (units ms, s, m, h, d)                │
│   Send-time values        │   $isoFromUnix(seconds)         the Unix seconds as an RFC 3339 time                                                             │
│   Lua scripts             │   $unixFromIso(time)            the RFC 3339 time as Unix seconds                                                                │
│   Lua catalog             │   $upper(text)                  the text in upper case                                                                           │
│                           │   $lower(text)                  the text in lower case                                                                           │
│                           │   $trim(text)                   the text without the spaces at the ends                                                          │
